.SS "Minor Changes"
.IP "\(bu" 2
In order to move towards stricter TypeScript support in the future, we're aiming to replace current usages of \fRany\fP with \fRunknown\fP on exposed typings for user-provided data\&. To do this in Remix v2 without introducing breaking changes in React Router v6, we have added generics to a number of shared types\&. These continue to default to \fRany\fP in React Router and are overridden with \fRunknown\fP in Remix\&. In React Router v7 we plan to move these to \fRunknown\fP as a breaking change\&. (\fR#10843\fP)
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRLocation\fP now accepts a generic for the \fRlocation\&.state\fP value
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRActionFunctionArgs\fP/\fRActionFunction\fP/\fRLoaderFunctionArgs\fP/\fRLoaderFunction\fP now accept a generic for the \fRcontext\fP parameter (only used in SSR usages via \fRcreateStaticHandler\fP)
.IP "  \(bu" 4
The return type of \fRuseMatches\fP (now exported as \fRUIMatch\fP) accepts generics for \fRmatch\&.data\fP and \fRmatch\&.handle\fP - both of which were already set to \fRunknown\fP
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
Move the \fR@private\fP class export \fRErrorResponse\fP to an \fRUNSAFE_ErrorResponseImpl\fP export since it is an implementation detail and there should be no construction of \fRErrorResponse\fP instances in userland\&. This frees us up to export a \fRtype ErrorResponse\fP which correlates to an instance of the class via \fRInstanceType\fP\&. Userland code should only ever be using \fRErrorResponse\fP as a type and should be type-narrowing via \fRisRouteErrorResponse\fP\&. (\fR#10811\fP)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Export \fRShouldRevalidateFunctionArgs\fP interface (\fR#10797\fP)
.IP "\(bu" 2
Removed private/internal APIs only required for the Remix v1 backwards compatibility layer and no longer needed in Remix v2 (\fR_isFetchActionRedirect\fP, \fR_hasFetcherDoneAnything\fP) (\fR#10715\fP)
.PP
