.SS "Minor Changes"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Move \fR\fRReact\&.startTransition\fP\fP usage behind a \fRfuture flag\fP to avoid issues with existing incompatible \fRSuspense\fP usages\&. We recommend folks adopting this flag to be better compatible with React concurrent mode, but if you run into issues you can continue without the use of \fRstartTransition\fP until v7\&. Issues usually boils down to creating net-new promises during the render cycle, so if you run into issues you should either lift your promise creation out of the render cycle or put it behind a \fRuseMemo\fP\&. (\fR#10596\fP)

.PP
Existing behavior will no longer include \fRReact\&.startTransition\fP:

.PP
.PP
.nf
<BrowserRouter>
  <Routes>{/*\&.\&.\&.*/}</Routes>
</BrowserRouter>

<RouterProvider router={router} />
.fi
.PP

.PP
If you wish to enable \fRReact\&.startTransition\fP, pass the future flag to your component:

.PP
.PP
.nf
<BrowserRouter future={{ v7_startTransition: true }}>
  <Routes>{/*\&.\&.\&.*/}</Routes>
</BrowserRouter>

<RouterProvider router={router} future={{ v7_startTransition: true }}/>
.fi
.PP

